Add algebra::close

Saturates a Structure under functionality and signature-imposed typing.
Structure now carries an eqlog_runtime::Unification<ElId> tracking
equality between elements, and els turns into a
BTreeMap<ElId, Option<ConcreteType>> where a ConcreteType pairs a
non-optional TypeId with its parent-model elements. After close, only
equivalence-class roots remain as els keys and every FuncApp, PredApp,
var-el value and ConcreteType.parents reference points at a canonical
root.

Close runs the fixed point of two passes until both settle:
functionality rebuilds func_apps with canonical keys and unions
duplicate results, and typing walks every func/pred app and imposes
the type the signature demands on each argument (and on the result,
for funcs). Unifying two elements also unifies the parents of their
types and reports a TypeConflict when types disagree. Close is not
yet wired into build.rs; the caller will translate TypeConflicts into
user-facing errors.
